<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">22</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-versinikia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-versinikia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Versinikia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 813</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Versinikia was fought on 22 June 813 near Versinikia, not far from Adrianople in Thrace.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ellendun"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-ellendun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ellendun</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 825</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ellendun was fought in 825 near Wroughton in Wiltshire, England, between Ecgberht of Wessex and Beornwulf of Mercia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hingston-down"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-hingston-down.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Hingston Down</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 838</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Hingston Down was fought in 838 at Hingston Down in east Cornwall, near the River Tamar, where Ecgberht of Wessex defeated a combined army of Cornish…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fontenoy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-fontenoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Fontenoy</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 841 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Fontenoy was fought in 841 CE in Burgundy between the Carolingian emperor Lothair I and his brothers Louis the German and Charles the Bald.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-clavijo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-clavijo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Clavijo</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 844 (legendary)</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Clavijo is a legendary battle said to have been fought in 844 near Clavijo in La Rioja, in which Ramiro I of Asturias defeated a Muslim army with the help…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tablada"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Tablada</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 844</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Tablada was fought in November 844 near Seville, where the army of the Umayyad emir Abd al-Rahman II defeated Viking raiders who had sacked the city.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ballon"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ballon</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 845</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ballon was fought on 22 November 845 near Bains-sur-Oust in eastern Brittany, between the Breton ruler Nominoe and the West Frankish king Charles the Bald.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ostia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-ostia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ostia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 849</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ostia was fought in 849 off Ostia, the port of Rome, between Muslim raiders from North Africa and an allied fleet from Naples, Amalfi, Gaeta and Sorrento.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-aclea"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Aclea</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 851</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Aclea was fought in 851 between the West Saxons under King Æthelwulf and his son Æthelbald and a large Viking army that had sacked Canterbury and London.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jengland"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Jengland</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 851</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Jengland was fought in August 851 near Grand-Fougeray on the border of Brittany, between Erispoe, son of the Breton ruler Nominoe, and the West Frankish…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-albelda"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-albelda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Albelda</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 859</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Albelda was fought in 859 near Albelda in La Rioja, northern Spain, where King Ordoño I of Asturias defeated Musa ibn Musa of the Banu Qasi, the dominant…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lalakaon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-lalakaon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Lalakaon</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 863</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Lalakaon was fought on 3 September 863 in Paphlagonia, in northern Asia Minor, between a Byzantine army under Petronas and the forces of Umar al-Aqta…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ashdown"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-ashdown.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ashdown</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 871</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ashdown was fought on 8 January 871 between the West Saxons, led by King Æthelred I and his brother Alfred, and the Great Heathen Army of the Danes.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bathys-ryax"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-bathys-ryax.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Bathys Ryax</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 872 or 878</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Bathys Ryax was fought in central Anatolia between the Byzantine army of Emperor Basil I and the Paulicians of Tephrike, probably in 872 or 878.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hafrsfjord"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-hafrsfjord.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Hafrsfjord</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 872</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Hafrsfjord was a naval battle in the fjord near present-day Stavanger in Rogaland, traditionally dated around 872 but possibly later.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dayr-al-aqul"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Dayr al-Aqul</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 876</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Dayr al-Aqul was fought in 876 on the Tigris south-east of Baghdad.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-edington"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-edington.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Edington</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 878</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Edington was fought in May 878 in Wiltshire, England, between the West Saxons under Alfred the Great and the Viking army of Guthrum.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-polvoraria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-polvoraria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Polvoraria</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 878</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Polvoraria was fought in 878 near the confluence of the Órbigo and Esla rivers in León, where the forces of Alfonso III of Asturias defeated an army of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sripurambiyam"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Sripurambiyam</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 885</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Sripurambiyam was fought around 885 near Kumbakonam in the Kaveri delta, when the Pallava king Aparajita and his ally Prithvipati I of the Western Gangas…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-questembert"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Questembert</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 888</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Questembert was fought around 888 or 890 near Questembert in southern Brittany, where Alan, count of Vannes, later called Alan the Great, defeated a large…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poley"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Poley</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 891</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Poley was fought in 891 near Poley, the modern town of Aguilar de la Frontera south of Córdoba, between the army of the Umayyad emir Abd Allah and the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bulgarophygon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-bulgarophygon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Bulgarophygon</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 896</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Bulgarophygon was fought in 896 near the town of that name in eastern Thrace, now Babaeski in Turkey.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-civil-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/carolingian-civil-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Carolingian civil war</span><span class="enc-type">War · 840–843</span><span class="enc-snip">The Carolingian civil war (840–843) was fought among the sons of Emperor Louis the Pious over the Frankish empire after his death in 840.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-bulgarian-war-of-894-896"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/byzantine-bulgarian-war-of-894-896.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Byzantine–Bulgarian war of 894–896</span><span class="enc-type">War · 894–896</span><span class="enc-snip">The Byzantine–Bulgarian war of 894–896 was fought between the Bulgarian Empire under Simeon I and the Byzantine Empire of Leo VI, after the Bulgarian market in…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-invasions-of-europe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hungarian-invasions-of-europe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hungarian invasions of Europe</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · c. 899–970</span><span class="enc-snip">The Hungarian invasions of Europe were the raids made by the Magyars from the Carpathian Basin into Germany, Italy, France and the Balkans between about 899 and 970.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Revolts &amp; revolutions <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-arrabal"><span class="enc-name">Revolt of the Arrabal</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 818</span><span class="enc-snip">The Revolt of the Arrabal was a rising in 818 of the people of the southern suburb (rabad) of Córdoba against the Umayyad emir al-Hakam I, fuelled by taxation and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/field-of-lies"><span class="enc-name">Field of Lies</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 833 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Field of Lies was the place near Colmar where, in 833 CE, the army of Emperor Louis the Pious deserted to his rebellious sons.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/zanj-rebellion"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zanj-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Zanj Rebellion</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 869–883</span><span class="enc-snip">The Zanj Rebellion was a major revolt in southern Iraq from 869 to 883, led by Ali ibn Muhammad and involving enslaved East Africans, known as the Zanj, who laboured in…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/huang-chao-rebellion"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/huang-chao-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Huang Chao Rebellion</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 874–884</span><span class="enc-snip">The Huang Chao Rebellion was a large uprising in China from 874 to 884, led by the salt smuggler Huang Chao.</span></a></li></ul></section>
